    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "Thank you. You know, we've heard from Kaiser Family Foundation Pew Research Center, other pollsters, as they've looked at those who are in the movable middle, those who are waiting to make a decision who have some outstanding concerns, plus those the 13, 14% who are pretty dug in and opposed to taking vaccine that there's There's a great concern at trying to connect to evangelical and conservative voters, particularly those in rural males are a particular concern. And I've been encouraged that the very well-known Republican pollster, Frank Luntz, has joined with Brian Castrucci doing a series of focus groups that have been very illuminating and have also enlisted those who were MDs within Congress Republican MDs to come together and they begun doing public service announcements. I mean, we're seeing leadership at the Republican level to coming from various directions to try and get the message out and connect and understand what those concerns are in terms of what are the concerns of those who are on the fence.",
