    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "So, we have pockets, the population if you actually looked at it. Honestly, it tends to be collectively, you know, a portion of the population is a little bit not as well off, not as well educated lives and more isolated and sometimes even more homogeneous type community. So, you know, there's some things to think through here, but the bottom line. It's pretty simple to me. This works. It's saving lives. It's a remarkable achievement. And, you know, I respect people that have a different opinion on these sorts of things and recognize that the United States is a free country and you have lots of freedom. I do think we need to have a pretty aggressive public advocacy here for you know, using these vaccines. And hopefully that will continue. You find very few responsible political leaders on either side that don't make the point. This is something you should do. And so I've been pleased with that in a divided time that on this we've been speaking pretty much with one voice.",
