  {
    "episode_id": 74275,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74275.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 22,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, I think that's correct. I think it's actually being spent quite well. You know, actually the Labor Age subcommittee on approach has been focused on this for a while. We actually had some hearings before the pandemic on the need to update our diagnostics all across the country in terms of getting information more rapidly being able to track disease. what it was going to take. I wish we'd had those hearings a couple of years ago. Maybe we would have been a little bit better prepared and provided information. But we do have an important opportunity here to capitalize the public health care system. I was pretty stunned years ago when I became the chairman of the subcommittee to find out my own state over 60% of the public health budget was coming from the CDC. The state just simply wasn't doing its part. I think the national number is about 50%. We have some states, New York usually is a real leader in this area, long tradition",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
