    "turn_idx": 46,
    "turn_text": "It's very important and I was kind of surprised in the Biden budget. There's actually a proposed cut. We have a particular agency in defense that thinks about pandemic disease and helps plan for it. And its budget was cut by like 40%. Now, I don't think that's because the Biden administration doesn't think this is important. I think they do think it's important. Every other investment, you know, on the civilian side shows that they think it's important. I think they just to cut the defense budgets or, you know, clamp down enough that people are trying to, I mean, the main mission of defense is obviously a military one and you have to have a military capable of engaging and defeating a near-peer opponents any place in the world. And I don't think we're funding that adequately in the president's proposal in my view. And I think some of these other areas then get squeezed, but they're important areas. And the Defense Department does house some capabilities that nobody else has. And we see it, again, it's main mission. It's always to fight and win wars. Nothing should take away from that. But having the ability, for instance, when we had the tsunamis in Indonesia to respond, having the ability to help our friends and allies of Japanese when they had their tsunami flash nuclear problems. We deployed 19,000 US military personnel to assist the Japanese government in the relief of its people. This is an advanced and capable country and a country that is very important to our own defense and a very firm",
